3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The answer is the Event Loop. And once you understand it, Node.js will never feel like magic again. Let me explain what the event loop

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
is and why Node.js needs it - without diving into confusing internal phases. What Problem Does the Event Loop Solve? The Single-Thread Limitation Node.js runs

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:50,000
your JavaScript on one thread. One thread means one thing at a time. The problem: What happens when a line of code takes a long

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
